# Draft knowledge entry: Boost CMake shared links should avoid OHOS SDK lld when CI lacks libxml2
id: DRAFT-boost-ohos-gnu-ld-for-cmake-shared-links
trigger_tool: cmake|conan|clang|lld
phase: build|consumer-link
error_signature: "Boost|cmake.build|libboost_.*\\.so|Error loading shared library libxml2\\.so\\.16|Error relocating .*llvm/bin/lld: xml.* symbol not found|clang-15: error: unable to execute command"

severity: 3
category: boost|cmake|linking|ohos|ci
match_keywords: Boost, CMakeToolchain, CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS, CMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS, CMAKE_MODULE_LINKER_FLAGS, lld, libxml2.so.16, fuse-ld

title: Boost CMake recipes on OHOS should force GNU ld for shared-library and consumer links
root_cause: >
  The OHOS SDK lld executable is dynamically linked against libxml2.so.16. CI jobs may run the
  package build without an interactive LD_LIBRARY_PATH that exposes the SDK LLVM library directory,
  so clang reaches the link step but lld itself fails to start before any Boost symbol resolution.
affected_scope: >
  Boost CMake-based Conan recipes that build shared libraries on HarmonyOS PC, including
  Boost.Python dependency packages and their CMake test_package consumers.
verification_cmd: |
  CI_PACKAGES="archives/b/boost/1.90.0.2.1" CI_BRANCH="feat/boost-1.90.0.2.1" CI_PR_NUMBER="6712" zsh ci/conan/build_and_test.sh

rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: force-gnu-ld-through-cmake-linker-flags
rec_description: >
  For OHOS builds, pass -fuse-ld=/data/service/hnp/bin/ld through CMakeToolchain linker flags for
  executable, shared-library, and module targets. Apply the same flag to test_package CMake builds
  so consumer link validation is independent of shell startup files.
rec_command: |
  gnu_ld_flag = "-fuse-ld=/data/service/hnp/bin/ld"
  for linker_flag in (
      "CMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS",
      "CMAKE_SHARED_LINKER_FLAGS",
      "CMAKE_MODULE_LINKER_FLAGS",
  ):
      tc.variables[linker_flag] = gnu_ld_flag
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: conan-cmaketoolchain-linker-flags

fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: prepend-sdk-llvm-libdir-for-diagnosis-only
fallback_description: >
  Temporarily prepending the SDK llvm/lib directory to LD_LIBRARY_PATH can confirm the lld/libxml2
  diagnosis, but it is weaker as a recipe fix because CI wrappers intentionally sanitize
  interactive shell variables.
fallback_command: |
  export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/data/service/hnp/ohos-sdk.org/ohos-sdk_26.0.0.18/ohos/native/llvm/lib:${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:-}
  /data/service/hnp/ohos-sdk.org/ohos-sdk_26.0.0.18/ohos/native/llvm/bin/lld --version
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: environment-diagnosis

forbid_1_pattern: "rely only on ~/.zshrc|interactive LD_LIBRARY_PATH|source setup before every CI build"
forbid_1_reason: Official CI may not load interactive shell state, so the recipe must carry link behavior itself.
forbid_1_consequence: The package can pass a local shadow run but fail official CI at the first shared-library link.
forbid_2_pattern: "patch Boost sources around xml symbols|copy libxml2 into the package"
forbid_2_reason: The failure is the host linker executable's runtime dependency, not a Boost source or package runtime dependency.
forbid_2_consequence: Such changes either do not affect clang's linker invocation or incorrectly mix a toolchain dependency into the Boost package.

principles: recipe-owned-build-environment, real-consumer-link, ci-portable-linker-selection
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to: E106, E120, E132
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of: eigenpy-3.13.0

